// Example.xcconfig — TMDB credentials template. Safe to commit.
//
// Quick start (from the repo root):
//   1. Sign up for free TMDB API access: https://www.themoviedb.org/settings/api
//   2. Copy this file to .secret/Secrets.xcconfig and enter the credentials below:
//        mkdir -p .secret && cp Shared/Example.xcconfig .secret/Secrets.xcconfig
//   3. Build & run — no runtime API-key entry is needed.
//
// How it flows: Secrets.xcconfig -> Info.plist (TMDBReadAccessToken = $(TMDB_READ_ACCESS_TOKEN))
// -> read at runtime and sent as an Authorization: Bearer header (see TMDBService).
// .secret/ is gitignored and its contents must never be committed.
TMDB_READ_ACCESS_TOKEN =

// Legacy fallback: the short v3 "API Key", sent as an api_key URL query parameter.
// Only used when TMDB_READ_ACCESS_TOKEN is empty; prefer the read access token above.
TMDB_API_KEY =

// Optional: enables explicit online subtitle searches through Wyzie Subs.
// Claim a free key at https://store.wyzie.io/redeem, then copy this file to
// .secret/Secrets.xcconfig and enter it below. Without a key, online subtitle
// search shows a setup state while the rest of Edendale continues to work.
WYZIE_API_KEY =

// Optional: cloud storage sources (Settings → Link Source). Each value is a
// public client identifier, not a secret — PKCE sign-in needs no client
// secret, and none ships anywhere — but they stay out of the repository with
// the other credentials. An empty value hides that provider in the build.
// See README.md → "Storage providers" for registering each app.
//   Google: an OAuth client of type iOS for bundle ID com.BaBaSaMa.Edendale,
//     e.g. 1234567890-abc123.apps.googleusercontent.com
//   Microsoft: the Application (client) ID of an Entra public client app
//   Dropbox: the App key of a scoped app with Full Dropbox access
GOOGLE_DRIVE_CLIENT_ID =
ONEDRIVE_CLIENT_ID =
DROPBOX_APP_KEY =
